[{"figure_index": 1, "page_no": 4, "caption": "Figure 1: BFT enhances the outputs of DeepSeek-R1-Distill series (14B, 32B and 70B). a : In the medical domain, theme-wise evaluation. b : In the medical domain, axis-wise evaluation. c : Forgetting evaluation in the general domain. We evaluated the general capabilities of LLMs previously fine-tuned on the OpenAI Health Bench Consensus subset using the MMLU benchmark. d : Forgetting evaluation in the general domain. We evaluated the general capabilities of LLMs previously fine-tuned on the OpenAI Health Bench Consensus subset using the CMMLU benchmark. e : In the biology domain, we applied BFT (blue) and SFT (orange) to fine-tune DeepSeek-R1-Distill series (14B, 32B and 70B). We evaluated LLMs on three biological process reasoning benchmarks. We evaluate ROUGE scores (recall-oriented understudy for gisting evaluation) between the generated final pathway names and ground truths, specifically ROUGE-L (longest common subsequence), ROUGE-1 (1-gram) and ROUGE-2 (2-gram) scores. f : We compared the BFT-based DeepSeek-R1-Distill (70B) against the latest baselines for biological process reasoning.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure composed of bar charts comparing model performance across tasks, model sizes, datasets, and methods.\n\nVisible panels and labels:\n- Panel **a**: Three grouped bar charts titled **Theme-wise (70B)**, **Theme-wise (32B)**, and **Theme-wise (14B)**. Y-axis is **Score**. X-axis compares **BFT** and **SFT**. Legend includes themes: `emergency_referrals`, `communication`, `hedging`, `complex_responses`, `health_data_tasks`, `global_health`, and `context_seeking`.\n- Panel **b**: Three grouped bar charts titled **Axis-wise (70B)**, **Axis-wise (32B)**, and **Axis-wise (14B)**. Y-axis is **Score**. X-axis compares **BFT** and **SFT**. Legend includes axes: `communication_quality`, `instruction_following`, `accuracy`, `context_awareness`, and `completeness`.\n- Panel **c**: Three grouped bar charts titled **MMLU (70B)**, **MMLU (32B)**, and **MMLU (14B)**. Y-axis is **Accuracy**. Categories include **STEM**, **Sociology**, **Humanities**, and **Other**. Legend compares **Base**, **BFT**, and **SFT**.\n- Panel **d**: Three grouped bar charts titled **CMMLU (70B)**, **CMMLU (32B)**, and **CMMLU (14B)**. Y-axis is **Accuracy**. Categories include **STEM**, **Sociology**, **Humanities**, and **Other**. Legend compares **Base**, **BFT**, and **SFT**.\n- Panel **e**: Nine grouped bar charts for summarization-style metrics across model sizes **14B**, **32B**, and **70B**. Metrics are **Rouge-L**, **Rouge-1**, and **Rouge-2**. X-axis datasets include **MsigDB**, **NeST**, and **Gene Ontology**. Legend compares **BFT** and **SFT**.\n- Panel **f**: Three grouped bar charts titled **MsigDB**, **NeST**, and **Gene Ontology**. Metrics on the x-axis are **Rouge-L**, **Rouge-1**, and **Rouge-2**. Legend compares methods **BFT**, **GeneAgent**, and **GPT-Hu**. Error bars are shown.\n\nBiological source objects:\n- The figure explicitly references biological or biomedical knowledge sources/datasets: **MSigDB**, **NeST**, and **Gene Ontology**.\n- No microscopy images, organisms, cells, tissues, molecules, or anatomical structures are visually shown.\n\nTransformations/model interfaces:\n- The figure compares model variants and training/finetuning conditions labeled **Base**, **BFT**, and **SFT** across model sizes **14B**, **32B**, and **70B**.\n- It presents quantitative evaluation outputs as grouped bar plots with accuracy, score, and ROUGE metrics.\n\nFindings visible from the figure:\n- Theme-wise and axis-wise scores vary substantially by model size and training condition.\n- MMLU and CMMLU accuracy are compared across subject groups for Base, BFT, and SFT.\n- ROUGE-based performance is shown for biomedical/gene-related datasets, with BFT and SFT compared in panel e and BFT/GeneAgent/GPT-Hu compared with error bars in panel f."]}, {"figure_index": 2, "page_no": 6, "caption": "Figure 2: BFT learns representations with biological meaning. a : UMAP visualization of gene embeddings. From left to right are the gene embeddings of scGPT, the text embeddings of gene descriptions output by OpenAI ChatGPT, and the text embeddings of gene descriptions output by BFT-based DeepSeek-R1-Distill 70B. b : Representation evaluation at the gene level, with the task type being single-gene input. The classifier takes a single gene embedding as input and predicts its biological attributes, such as long-range and short-range transcription factors, dosage-sensitive and dosage-insensitive transcription factors, bivalent and Lys4-only methylated genes, and bivalent and non-methylated genes. c : Representation evaluation at the gene level, with the task type being multi-gene input. The embeddings of two genes or two proteins are concatenated, and the classifier predicts their interaction type. d : Representation evaluation at the cell level. On single-cell data, cell embeddings are obtained by aggregating gene embeddings, and the evaluation includes phenotypes and cell types. e : Comparison of multimodal integration at the cell level, with the goal of integrating the two modalities of RNA and ADT. The three main columns (Bio conservation, Batch correction, and Aggregate score) respectively represent biological heterogeneity, modality mixing degree, and the overall metric. Each main column contains specific sub-metrics. For the first two columns, the color gradient from purple to green indicates scores from low to high. f : Comparison of single-cell perturbation response prediction results, with zero-shot prediction conducted on four perturbation datasets respectively.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure comparing gene/cell embedding or foundation-model methods.\n\nVisible panels:\n\n- **Panel a**: Three UMAP/t-SNE-like 2D embedding plots labeled **scGPT**, **GenePT**, and **BFT**. Points are colored by gene biotype annotations. Legend includes biological source objects/classes such as **IG_V_gene**, **IG_V_pseudogene**, **TR_J_gene**, **TR_V_gene**, **antisense**, **lncRNA**, **miRNA**, **misc_RNA**, **polymorphic_pseudogene**, **processed_pseudogene**, **processed_transcript**, **protein_coding**, **pseudogene**, **rRNA**, **sense_intronic**, **snRNA**, **snoRNA**, **transcribed_unprocessed_pseudogene**, and **unprocessed_pseudogene**. The embeddings show different clustering/separation patterns across models.\n\n- **Panel b**: Bar chart titled **Single gene input**, y-axis **AUC**, comparing methods **scGPT**, **GenePT**, and **BFT** across tasks: **TF range**, **Dosage sensitivity**, **Bivalent vs non-bivalent**, and **Bivalent vs Utx**. BFT appears highest or near-highest for several tasks, with numeric AUC labels above bars.\n\n- **Panel c**: Bar chart titled **Multi gene input**, y-axis **AUC**, comparing **scGPT**, **GenePT**, and **BFT** on **GO** and **PPI** tasks. BFT has the highest visible scores in both categories.\n\n- **Panel d**: Two grouped bar charts for clustering metrics. Top: **Clustering performance (phenotype)** with metrics **ARI**, **AMI**, **ASW**. Bottom: **Clustering performance (cell type)** with the same metrics. Methods shown are **PCA**, **scGPT**, **GenePT**, and **BFT**. BFT shows the strongest visible clustering scores, especially for cell type AMI.\n\n- **Panel e**: Table-like benchmark summary comparing integration methods **scMODAL**, **BFT**, **Harmony**, and **BBKNN**. Columns are grouped into **Bio conservation**, **Batch correction**, and **Aggregate score**. Metrics include **Isolated labels**, **KMeans NMI**, **KMeans ARI**, **Silhouette label**, **CLISI**, **Silhouette batch**, **iLISI**, **KBET**, **Graph connectivity**, **PCR comparison**, plus aggregate **Batch correction**, **Bio conservation**, and **Total**. Colored circles and bars encode scores. **scMODAL** has the highest total score shown.\n\n- **Panel f**: Four small bar charts labeled **hepg2**, **rpe1**, **jurkat**, and **k562**. Y-axis is **Score**. Categories include **DES**, **PDS**, and **MAE**. Methods in the legend: **BFT**, **STATE-SE**, and **STATE-small**. Bars include error bars. The plots compare method performance across cell-line contexts.\n\nOverall finding shown visually: the figure benchmarks multiple models/methods, especially **BFT**, **scGPT**, **GenePT**, **scMODAL**, **Harmony**, **BBKNN**, and **STATE** variants, across gene embedding structure, gene-level prediction AUCs, clustering metrics, multimodal/batch integration scores, and perturbation or cell-line prediction scores."]}, {"figure_index": 3, "page_no": 13, "caption": "Extended Data Figure 1: Ablation study. a : Test results on different mathematical reasoning datasets. We set two baselines: the red dashed line represents SFT, and the blue dashed line represents reinforcement learning (represented by GRPO). BFT includes three window length settings (BFT-128, BFT-256, and BFT-512). BFT w/o sample denotes removing the sample-level weighting mechanism from BFT (this setting does not require a sliding window). BFT w/o token denotes removing the token-level weighting mechanism from BFT (this setting requires a sliding window). b : Tracking the reasoning performance of BFT (with different window length settings) within 1 training epoch.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel quantitative figure with panels labeled **a** and **b**.\n\nPanel **a** shows three bar charts for benchmark accuracy:\n- **math_oai**\n- **minerva_math**\n- **olympiadbench**\n\nEach chart has y-axis **Accuracy (%)** and x-axis methods including **SFT**, **GRPO**, **BFT-128**, **BFT-256**, **BFT-512**, **BFT w/o sample**, and token-ablation variants such as **BFT-128 w/o token**, **BFT-256 w/o token**, **BFT-512 w/o token**. Dashed horizontal reference lines indicate **GRPO baseline** in blue and **SFT baseline** in red.\n\nPanel **b** shows three line plots for the same benchmarks, plotting **Accuracy (%)** versus **Global Step**. Curves compare **BFT-128**, **BFT-256**, and **BFT-512**, with a legend below.\n\nNo biological source objects, microscopy images, anatomical structures, or biological transformations are visible. The figure appears to report machine learning or reasoning-model benchmark results. The visible finding is that BFT variants generally improve over SFT and approach or exceed GRPO baseline performance, with performance varying by benchmark, BFT size, token ablation, and training step."]}, {"figure_index": 4, "page_no": 14, "caption": "Extended Data Figure 2: The training runtime (unit: seconds) and evaluation scores of different methods. BFT includes three window length settings (128, 256, and 512), and the comparison methods include SFT and Focal loss. The training runtime of BFT is close to that of SFT, while its evaluation score is far higher than that of SFT.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a single-panel scatter/bubble plot comparing methods by `Runtime` on the x-axis and `Score` on the y-axis. Points are color-coded by `Method`, with a legend listing `SFT`, `Focal loss`, `BFT-256`, `BFT-128`, and `BFT-512`. Bubble size represents `Metrics`, with a separate size legend showing values approximately `0.016`, `0.038`, `0.093`, `0.106`, and `0.111`.\n\nVisible findings:\n- `BFT-256` has the highest score, labeled about `0.111`, at runtime around `9880`.\n- `BFT-512` is slightly lower, labeled about `0.106`, at runtime around `9820`.\n- `BFT-128` is labeled about `0.093`, at runtime around `9750`.\n- `SFT` is much lower, labeled about `0.038`, at runtime around `9670`.\n- `Focal loss` is lowest, labeled about `0.016`, at runtime around `11050`.\n\nNo biological source objects, microscopy/image transformations, or model interface diagrams are visible."]}, {"figure_index": 5, "page_no": 16, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["S