-dimensional cell embeddings for `M` cells. No specific organism, dataset, model name, or empirical finding is visible in the image."]}, {"figure_index": 7, "page_no": 17, "caption": "Extended Data Figure 7: UMAP visualization of the multi-gene input task. a : For GGI, the input embedding of the classifier is directly concatenated from the embeddings of two genes. b : For PPI, the input embedding of the classifier is directly concatenated from the embeddings of two proteins.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure with two labeled rows, `a` and `b`, comparing embedding visualizations from three models: `scGPT`, `GenePT`, and `BFT`.\n\nPanel `a` shows UMAP scatter plots titled `Gene Pairs Colored by Interaction Label` for `scGPT` and `GenePT`, and `Protein Pairs Colored by Interaction Label` for `BFT`. Points are colored by binary interaction label: blue `0` and orange `1`. Axes are labeled `UMAP1` and `UMAP2`. The plots show different spatial separations of positive and negative interaction pairs across the three model-derived embeddings.\n\nPanel `b` shows UMAP scatter plots titled `Protein Pairs Colored by Interaction Label` for `scGPT`, `GenePT`, and `BFT`. Points are colored by interaction category labels: `activation`, `binding`, `catalysis`, `expression`, `inhibition`, `ptmod`, and `reaction`. Axes are again labeled `UMAP1` and `UMAP2`. The biological source objects are gene pairs and protein pairs, transformed into low-dimensional UMAP embeddings from model representations. The visible comparison suggests that the models organize interaction pairs differently, with BFT showing more structured separated clusters in panel `b` than the more compact or diffuse scGPT and GenePT protein-pair plots."]}, {"figure_index": 8, "page_no": 17, "caption": "Extended Data Figure 8: UMAP visualization of cell-level embeddings. a : PCA embeddings of the raw data, colored by cell type labels (cell type heterogeneity), patient labels (batch labels), and phenotype labels (disease heterogeneity), respectively. b : Cell embeddings derived from LLM-BFT, colored by cell type labels (cell type heterogeneity), patient labels (batch labels), and phenotype labels (disease heterogeneity), respectively.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure with two rows labeled **a** and **b**. Each row contains three UMAP scatter plots with axes labeled **UMAP1** and **UMAP2**.\n\nPanel **a**:\n- Three UMAP embeddings are shown for the same dataset or analysis view.\n- Left plot is colored by **celltype**, with legend entries including BCell, EC, Fibroblast, MSC, Mastcell, MonoMphDC, NK, Plasma, SMC1, SMC2, Tcell, and Unknown.\n- Middle plot is colored by **patient**, with affected samples **affected_1** through **affected_8** and controls **control_1** through **control_3**.\n- Right plot is colored by **phenotype**, with categories **Ascending only**, **Ascending to descending**, **Ascending w/ root**, and **Control**.\n- The plotted biological source objects appear to be single cells or cell/nucleus profiles embedded in 2D UMAP space.\n\nPanel **b**:\n- Three additional UMAP scatter plots with the same labeling scheme: **celltype**, **patient**, and **phenotype**.\n- The UMAP structure differs from panel a, showing larger, more continuous clusters.\n- The same cell-type and patient/phenotype legends are visible.\n- This likely represents another subset, preprocessing state, or embedding resolution, but the specific transformation is not stated in the image.\n\nVisible transformations/model interfaces:\n- Dimensionality reduction/embedding using **UMAP**.\n- Color mapping by metadata annotations: cell type, patient identity, and phenotype group.\n\nVisible findings:\n- Distinct cell-type clusters are present in UMAP space.\n- Patient identities and phenotype groups are distributed across multiple clusters rather than confined to a single visible region.\n- Some phenotype categories show enriched regions within parts of the embeddings, especially in the rightmost plots of both panels."]}, {"figure_index": 9, "page_no": 18, "caption": "Extended Data Figure 9: UMAP visualization of single-cell multimodal data integration results. Rows 1 to 4 represent different integration methods, respectively. Columns 1 to 3 correspond to different coloring labels (modality, cell type, and donor), respectively.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure showing UMAP embeddings for single-cell multimodal data integration/comparison.\n\nVisible structure:\n- 4 rows labeled: `BFT`, `BBKNN`, `Harmony`, `scMODAL`\n- 3 columns labeled: `modality`, `celltype`, `donor`\n- Each panel has axes labeled `UMAP1` and `UMAP2`\n\nPanel contents:\n- `modality` panels color points by assay/modality:\n  - `ADT` in blue\n  - `RNA` in orange\n- `celltype` panels color points by immune cell annotation:\n  - `B`\n  - `CD4 T`\n  - `CD8 T`\n  - `DC`\n  - `Mono`\n  - `NK`\n  - `other`\n  - `other T`\n- `donor` panels color points by donor/sample:\n  - `P1` through `P8`\n\nBiological source objects:\n- Single-cell measurements from immune cell populations.\n- Modalities shown are RNA and ADT, suggesting paired or integrated single-cell transcriptomic and antibody-derived tag data.\n- Donor labels indicate multiple biological samples or individuals.\n\nTransformations/model interfaces:\n- All panels show dimensionality reduction via UMAP.\n- Rows compare different batch correction or integration methods: BFT, BBKNN, Harmony, and scMODAL.\n- The same embeddings are visualized under different metadata colorings: modality, cell type, and donor.\n\nVisible findings:\n- `BFT` shows substantial overlap between ADT and RNA in the modality panel, with cell-type structure visible and donor colors mixed.\n- `BBKNN` shows stronger separation or structure by modality, with RNA and ADT occupying partially distinct regions.\n- `Harmony`